  "section_notes": "S1 requires 24-hour reporting of serious incidents but limits scope to serious categories and gives customer notice within 5 business days. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% failure limit but does not automatically stop sales above 5%, allowing regulator discretion. S3 mandates new-unit shut-off from adoption and a 6-year retrofit deadline for technically compatible units. S4 requires built-in fire suppression after 36 months. S5 mandates recall above 8 incidents/100k with prompt customer notices, but lacks a serious-injury clause."
